course: dictionary
lesson: 2364
title: The word cue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cue is a signal that tells you it is time to do something. Actors wait for their cue before they speak or walk onstage, so a cue can be a word, a sound or an action. «Cue the music!» means start the music now.
explain: A cue can also be a hint that helps you understand or remember something. Teachers talk about «context cues» and «picture cues» to help you work out a hard word. In «Cue cards with key words beat reading every word from a sheet», the cards are the hint that helps the speaker remember what to say next.
explain: As a verb, cue means to give a signal to start, or to get something ready to play at the right point. A cue can also be a long thin stick used in snooker and pool, so always check the sentence to find the right meaning.
fact: A cue is a signal that tells someone when to act.
fact: «On cue» means at exactly the right moment.
fact: «Take a cue from someone» means copy what they do.
fact: A cue can also be a hint, such as a «context cue» or a «picture cue».
fact: A pool cue is a long thin stick used to hit the ball.
exercise: «Actors learn the cue, the line just before theirs.» What is a cue in this sentence? | A hat worn on stage | A loud noise from the audience | *The line just before theirs, which tells them when to speak | A dance that ends the play
exercise: Which phrase means at exactly the right moment? | take a cue from | pool cue | *on cue | cue cards
exercise: «Cue cards hold key words only, so you can look up often.» What do the cards do? | They are a type of sheet you must read every word from | *They give you hints to help you remember | They play music for the class | They are a long thin stick for hitting a ball
test: «Cue the music!» What does cue mean in this sentence? | *To give a signal to start | To copy someone | To stop | To hit a ball with a stick
test: What is a picture cue? | A card with a song on it | A stick for hitting the ball | A signal to stop the play | *A picture that helps you work out a word
exam: «An elephant that lifts its ear on cue lets the vet take blood without a fight.» What does on cue mean here? | Slowly, with a big ear | Never, not once | *At exactly the right moment | Very loudly
